  "summary": "The original code suffered from a critical O(n²) performance bottleneck and potential prototype pollution vulnerabilities. I have refactored the logic to use a Map for O(n) time complexity and added JSDoc documentation with input validation to improve robustness and maintainability.",
  "fixed_code": "/**\n * Counts the frequency of each word in an array.\n * @param {string[]} words - Array of words to count.\n * @returns {Map<string, number>} A map of words to their frequency.\n */\nfunction countWordFrequencies(words) {\n    if (!Array.isArray(words)) return new Map();\n\n    const counts = new Map();\n    for (const word of words) {\n        counts.set(word, (counts.get(word) || 0) + 1);\n    }\n\n    return counts;\n}\n\nmodule.exports = { countWordFrequencies };"
